                <pb facs="0457" n="358" sameAs="frus:frus1936v05/pg358"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">825.5151/363: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State to the Ambassador in
                        Chile</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Philip</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1936-10-31T14:00:00-05:00">October 31, 1936—2
                        p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>75. Your telegram No. 108, October 30, 3 p.m. Please telegraph before Monday
                    morning the apparent reason for new gold rate and whether you regard it as
                    discriminatory against American goods because most imports affected come from
                    the United States or because a more favorable exchange rate is given imports of
                    the same commodities from compensation agreement countries.</p>
                <p>Also please telegraph any suggestions which you have as to form and content of
                    possible representations.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Carr</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
